12:["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Proof signal - one specific, credible data point"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"A number of customers, a recognisable logo, a specific result. Not a 5-star rating with no context - that is decoration, not proof. One specific, attributable proof element above the fold changes the trust calculus for a cold visitor."}]]}]
13:["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 mt-0.5 text-accent font-bold","children":[4,"."]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Primary CTA - visible without scrolling"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"One action. Label that describes the outcome of clicking, not the mechanics: \"Start my free trial\" not \"Submit.\" The CTA does not have to dominate the viewport - the headline carries more weight - but it must be findable without scrolling."}]]}]]}]
14:["$","li","4",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 mt-0.5 text-accent font-bold","children":[5,"."]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Risk-reducer - something that lowers the cost of action"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"\"No credit card required.\" \"Cancel any time.\" A money-back guarantee. Something specific that lowers the perceived risk of taking the CTA action. \"Risk-free\" alone is marketing copy - it does not answer the question of what risk-free means in practice."}]]}]]}]
15:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"If any of these five are missing or positioned below the fold, you have a structural conversion leak that no amount of targeting optimisation will fix."}]
16:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"The most common above-fold failures"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"These are the patterns that consistently show up as conversion leaks on paid traffic landing pages. They are not subtle design errors - they are structural choices that make the above-fold section do no selling work at all."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-5 space-y-4 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","li","Company name or tagline as H1",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-4 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Company name or tagline as H1"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed","children":"\"Welcome to Acme Inc.\" and \"Transforming the Future of Work\" both fail the same test: a cold visitor cannot tell from either whether they are in the right place. The H1 is the most-read element on the page. Wasting it on a brand name or a vague aspiration is a first-impression failure."}]]}],["$","li","Generic hero image",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-4 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Generic hero image"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed","children":"A stock photo of a smiling team, an abstract gradient, or a product screenshot with no context consumes above-fold real estate without communicating anything. The image should reinforce the headline claim, not decorate it."}]]}],["$","li","CTA below the fold",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-4 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"CTA below the fold"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed","children":"On mobile at 390px, a CTA positioned 1,200px down the page might as well not exist for cold traffic. If the visitor has to scroll to find out what to do next, a portion of them will not scroll - they will use the back button."}]]}],["$","li","No proof in the first viewport",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-4 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"No proof in the first viewport"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed","children":"A page that asks for action before it gives evidence is asking for trust it has not earned. Even a single, specific social proof element above the fold changes the trust calculus. Generic badges and star ratings without context do not count."}]]}],["$","li","Competing visual weights",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-4 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Competing visual weights"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-1 leading-relaxed","children":"Multiple large elements at the same size, multiple CTAs, or a complex navigation bar all split attention and reduce the probability that the primary CTA is what the visitor's eye lands on. Simplifying the above-fold section - removing elements rather than adding them - is consistently the highest-leverage intervention for pages with visual hierarchy problems."}]]}]]}]]}]
17:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"The fold is different on every device - test both"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"“Above the fold” is not a fixed pixel height. On a 375px iPhone with browser chrome, the visible viewport is roughly 580px tall. On a 1024px laptop with a 72px navigation bar, it is approximately 950px. What appears above the fold in your desktop design tool may be deep below the fold on the phone your traffic is using."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The diagnostic protocol:"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-4 space-y-3 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],"Open your landing page in Chrome DevTools. Set device to iPhone 12 Pro (390×844). Screenshot what is visible without scrolling. Do all 5 required elements appear?"]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],"Repeat at 375px (iPhone SE / older Android). If layout breaks or key elements disappear, that is a specific technical fix, not a copy problem."]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],"Check 1024px for tablet/small laptop. CTA buttons tend to disappear at tablet breakpoints due to layout reflows."]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"If your paid traffic is primarily mobile - check your analytics; most paid social is - optimise for 375–390px first. Desktop performance is secondary to the device your visitors are actually using."}]]}]
18:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Visual hierarchy: the reading order is the sales sequence"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The eye does not read a landing page - it scans it. Size, contrast, and position determine reading order. That reading order shapes whether the above-fold section makes its argument in the right sequence."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Audit your visual hierarchy with this test: if a visitor reads only the three largest elements on your above-fold section, do they understand what you do, who it is for, and what to do next? If those three elements are your logo, a decorative image, and a generic tagline - your hierarchy is selling nothing."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The correct hierarchy for cold paid traffic is: headline → proof signal or subheadline → CTA. Everything else should be visually subordinate. When multiple elements compete at the same visual weight, the visitor's eye lands nowhere in particular - which means it is less likely to land on the CTA."}]]}]
19:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Speed and the fold: slow pages lose visitors before they see the first screen"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":["Above-fold optimisation only matters if the page loads fast enough for the above-fold section to be seen. A 2020 Deloitte/Google study of 37 retail, travel, and lead-generation brands found that a 0.1-second improvement in mobile load time increased retail conversions by 8.4% and travel conversions by 10.1%. The study's full methodology is available at"," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://www.thinkwithgoogle.com/_qs/documents/9757/Milliseconds_Make_Millions_report_hQYAbZJ.pdf","className":"text-accent hover:text-fg underline","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","children":"Think with Google: Milliseconds Make Millions"}],"."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":["According to the"," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://almanac.httparchive.org/en/2024/performance","className":"text-accent hover:text-fg underline","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","children":"2024 Web Almanac"}]," ","(HTTP Archive, Nov 2024), only 38% of mobile home pages passed all Core Web Vitals in 2024. That means more than six in ten mobile landing pages are failing Google's real-world performance thresholds - before the above-fold content is ever evaluated."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"If your LCP is above 2.5 seconds on mobile, fix load time before optimising above-fold layout. A visitor who abandons during load never sees your headline."}]]}]
