1b:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-6 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Frequently asked questions"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"What should be above the fold on a landing page?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Five elements: a headline that names the outcome and the audience, a subheadline that explains the mechanism, at least one specific proof signal, a primary CTA visible without scrolling, and a risk-reducer (guarantee, \"no credit card required\", or similar). If any of these are missing or below the fold, the above-fold section is not doing conversion work."}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"How do I know what is above the fold on mobile?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Open your landing page in Chrome DevTools, set the device to iPhone 12 Pro (390x844), and screenshot what is visible without scrolling. Do not use a browser emulator as a substitute for a real device test - emulators do not replicate browser chrome height, font rendering, or thumb reach. Repeat at 375px (iPhone SE) for older Android coverage."}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"Does above-the-fold content affect conversion rate?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Yes, directly. For cold paid traffic with no prior brand relationship, the above-fold section is the first and often only content they evaluate before deciding to stay or leave. If the headline does not confirm the ad promise, if no proof is visible, or if the CTA requires scrolling to find, a significant portion of paid traffic exits before seeing the rest of the page."}]]}],["$","div","3",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"Should I put the CTA above the fold?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"For cold paid traffic: yes. The CTA should be visible without scrolling. It does not have to be the dominant element - the headline and proof carry more weight - but the CTA needs to be findable in the first viewport. For warm traffic (email list, retargeting), the CTA below the fold is acceptable because those visitors are more likely to scroll. Segment your traffic type before deciding."}]]}],["$","div","4",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"What is the most common above-fold mistake on paid traffic landing pages?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Using the company name or tagline as the H1. \"Welcome to Acme Inc.\" and \"Transforming the Future of Work\" both fail the same test: a cold visitor cannot tell from either headline whether they are in the right place. The H1 is the most-read element on the page. It should state the specific outcome you deliver and who you deliver it to, in the same language the ad used to bring the visitor there."}]]}],"$L27","$L28","$L29"]}]]}]
1c:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-accent/40 bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Find the leak on your page"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The free Nebula audit checks all 9 signals and returns a prioritised list of what to fix first. The $97 One-Leak Repair Sprint supplies a tailored change for one high-confidence page-level finding. You or your developer implements it, and the 30-day re-audit verifies the page condition. It does not promise conversion lift."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap gap-4","children":[["$","$L10",null,{"href":"/audit?utm_source=learning-centre&utm_medium=organic-content","className":"inline-flex rounded bg-accent px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-bg hover:opacity-85 hover:bg-accent transition-colors","children":"Run the free audit"}],["$","$L10",null,{"href":"/pricing","className":"inline-flex rounded border border-accent px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-accent hover:bg-accent-dim transition-colors","children":"See the One-Leak Repair Sprint"}]]}]]}]
